    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0799" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.4121/283: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-02-15T13:00:00-05:00">February 15,
                            1936—1 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>55. Your despatch No. 1933, January 27. Draft Convention approved. Advise whether
                    full powers will be forwarded soon so convention can be sent to Senate during
                    present session.</p>
                <p>Inquire whether Foreign Office agrees with the Department that notices of
                    adherence given by the two Governments under the Convention of 1899 as
                    supplemented by the Convention of 1902<anchor n="84" xml:id="d565-f1"/> will
                    remain unaffected by the coming into operation of the present Convention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
